---
import { INSTALL_CLOUD_PATH, INSTALL_OWN_HARDWARE_PATH } from '../lib/links'
---

<section class="band" id="install">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="mos-eyebrow">Choose your platform</span>
      <h2 class="mos-section-title">Where should your cloud live?</h2>
      <p class="mos-body-lg mos-meta">A computer at home, a cloud server you rent, or (soon) one we run for you. Honest about what each one needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="paths">
      <div class="mos-panel path">
        <span class="mos-pill mos-pill-accent">Own hardware</span>
        <h3>USB installer</h3>
        <p class="mos-meta" style="font-size:0.92rem">Download the image, write it to a USB stick, boot a spare machine from it. One confirmation, a few minutes of copying, and the screen shows your suite's address.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A spare mini-PC or old laptop to dedicate — its disk is erased</li>
          <li>A free USB writer such as Rufus or balenaEtcher</li>
          <li>Best privacy: nothing leaves your home, and it costs only electricity</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="mos-link" href={INSTALL_OWN_HARDWARE_PATH}>Go to the install guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mos-panel path">
        <span class="mos-pill mos-pill-accent">Cloud server</span>
        <h3>One command</h3>
        <p class="mos-meta" style="font-size:0.92rem">Sign up with a provider, deploy a small Ubuntu 24.04 server, paste one command into its browser console and wait about ten minutes. Done. Nothing to install on your own computer, and a six-minute video walks you through every click.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A small rented server, about $20–25 a month</li>
          <li>Reachable from anywhere you allow</li>
          <li>Your own domain in one step, or the address MOS generates for you</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="mos-link" href={INSTALL_CLOUD_PATH}>Go to the install guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mos-panel path coming">
        <span class="mos-badge">Coming soon</span>{/* tracked: https://github.com/rpuls/my-own-suite/issues/279 */}
        <h3>Managed hosting</h3>
        <p class="mos-meta" style="font-size:0.92rem">Buy from MOS: one click provisions and runs a cloud server for you. No terminal, no VPS account.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Nothing to set up yourself</li>
          <li>MOS-provisioned and maintained</li>
          <li>A paid subscription — pricing announced at launch</li>
          <li>Planned — not yet available</li>{/* tracked: https://github.com/rpuls/my-own-suite/issues/279 */}
        </ul>
        <span class="mos-meta" style="font-size:0.86rem">We'll announce it here.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
